+The saturation controls can now be settled exactly at N=4,5 without relying on the finite bound of a power search. In the ring S_N[z], `(I_close,1-z*u)` and `(I_close,1-z*eta)` are unit ideals because u and eta vanish at every point. For the wrong localizers u+1, B, and w2, explicit points on the two families give nonzero values of the respective localizer, so the inverse-equation ideals are nonunit. For u+1 the origin works with z=1; for B use C_B at B=1; for w2 use C_3 at w2=1. This proves the non-vacuity of the same localization operation on the actual closing ideal. No `sat()` wrapper or component was misidentified; the rings and inverse equations are stated explicitly.
