+
+**9. The complete dependency chain, and its boundary hypothesis.**
+
+If U_eta were proved, specializing the universal jets to any terminal reconstruction with b != 0 would give eta=0 there, hence B*eta=0. In the terminal homogeneous ideal J_t this proves
+
+```
+B*eta in sqrt(J_t : b^infinity).
+```
+
+To obtain the unlocalized (R) from this assertion, one must additionally know
+
+```
+B*eta in sqrt(J_t+(b)) for every t and every field factor.       (BOUNDARY)
+```
+
+Indeed the exact radical decomposition is
+
+```
+sqrt(J_t)=sqrt(J_t:b^infinity) intersect sqrt(J_t+(b)).
+```
+
+The b=1 free-jet ring cannot prove the second factor merely by a normalization. As a logical control, in Q[b,eta] the ideal (b) becomes the unit ideal on inverting b, while eta is not in its original radical. This example is not asserted to be an (UF) solution; it demonstrates the missing algebraic implication. Xempty’s explicit b=0 treatment is why this issue is material to the stated residual, rather than hypothetical.
+
+With **both** U_eta and (BOUNDARY), the remainder of the charged dependency chain is:
+
+```
+B*eta in sqrt(J_t)                                  [(R)]
+ => tau in sqrt(I_+),
+    tau=-(g*y/3)*B*eta modulo I_+, g*y/3 a unit
