+That statement would exclude **all** further nonconstant b-nonzero solutions of actual degree at least four. It is sufficient for U_eta but is not necessary: additional components entirely inside eta=0 would preserve U_eta. Thus “the curve is the same for all N” is a stronger conjecture than the task’s target. The finite radical equalities and the uniform inclusion `C_B union C_3 subseteq V(I_close,N)` do not supply its reverse inclusion at an unbounded degree.
