+The b=1 free-jet ring cannot prove the second factor merely by a normalization. As a logical control, in Q[b,eta] the ideal (b) becomes the unit ideal on inverting b, while eta is not in its original radical. This example is not asserted to be an (UF) solution; it demonstrates the missing algebraic implication. Xempty’s explicit b=0 treatment is why this issue is material to the stated residual, rather than hypothetical.
